With `--recursive-modules`, Rust refinements may extend extern classes with foreign
members and generated functions, methods and constructors, including function-by-method
bodies, and introduce generic foreign classes. Trait parents use the ordinary Rust
implementation and upcast conventions, including inherited default methods and erased
ghost fields. Each class uses the refining module's foreign namespace. Generated
constructors execute after allocation through the foreign type's zero-argument hook.
Own and inherited compiled fields and foreign members with bodies retain explicit
rejections; a trait's proper methods must be wholly generated or wholly foreign.
